or agents on your data platform&#10;&#10;1️⃣ &#119825;&#119838;&#119852;&#119848;&#119854;&#119851;&#119836;&#119838; &#119814;&#119834;&#119853;&#119838;&#119856;&#119834;&#119858;&#10;Governed read path into warehouse tables &amp; metadata. Exposes reads as Resources, queries as Tools, and sanitises backend responses before the LLM sees them, so a prompt-injection payload hiding in a customer record can&apos;t hijack the agent.&#10;&#10;2️⃣ &#119827;&#119848;&#119848;&#119845; &#119822;&#119851;&#119836;&#119841;&#119838;&#119852;&#119853;&#119851;&#119834;&#119853;&#119848;&#119851;&#10;Bundles multi-step workflows into one composite tool call. "Provision this data product and notify the owner" becomes a single call instead of three that the agent has to sequence itself.&#10;&#10;3️⃣ &#119826;&#119853;&#119834;&#119853;&#119838;&#119839;&#119854;&#119845; &#119826;&#119838;&#119852;&#119852;&#119842;&#119848;&#119847; &#119826;&#119838;&#119851;&#119855;&#119838;&#119851;&#10;For multi-turn work, think in-progress query building or iterative transformations. A session ID carries context across calls, with the server maintaining state and expiring it on inactivity.&#10;&#10;4️⃣ &#119823;&#119851;&#119848;&#119857;&#119858; &#119808;&#119840;&#119840;&#119851;&#119838;&#119840;&#119834;&#119853;&#119848;&#119851; (MCP Router)&#10;Fronts many upstream servers as one endpoint. Merging all upstream tools into one flat list tanks LLM tool-selection accuracy. Scoped aggregation, surfacing only what&apos;s relevant per task, is what actually works. This is the backbone of enterprise MCP gateways.&#10;&#10;5️⃣ &#119811;&#119848;&#119846;&#119834;&#119842;&#119847;-&#119826;&#119849;&#119838;&#119836;&#119842;&#119839;&#119842;&#119836; &#119808;&#119837;&#119834;&#119849;&#119853;&#119838;&#119851; (Semantic Layer)&#10;The one most relevant to data teams. Wraps low-level APIs with human-readable descriptions, normalises natural-language inputs, resolves IDs to names, and translates errors into plain English. This is "semantic-layer-first MCP." "Revenue" and "Customer" mean one thing, defined once, regardless of which system the agent hits.&#10;&#10;&#10;&#128273; &#119809;&#119848;&#119847;&#119854;&#119852; &#119849;&#119834;&#119853;&#119853;&#119838;&#119851;&#119847;: Governed Discovery / Data-Product Marketplace&#10;Enforcing governance through data-product discovery in federated architectures, not just at the adapter layer. Worth flagging for anyone building a DataOS-native stack.&#10;&#10;&#10;&#128278; &#119819;&#119838;&#119834;&#119851;&#119847; &#119846;&#119848;&#119851;&#119838; &#119834;&#119835;&#119848;&#119854;&#119853; &#119853;&#119841;&#119842;&#119852; &#119851;&#119838;&#119852;&#119838;&#119834;&#119851;&#119836;&#119841;: https://lnkd.in/dMxSMzTU&#10;Which of these are you already running in production?&#10;&#10;&#10;#MCP #ModelContextProtocol #AIAgents' resource-id="com.linkedin.android:id/feed_render_item_text" class="android.widget.TextView" package="com.linkedin.android" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[0,665][1440,2856]" drawing-order="2" hint="" /></node></node></node></node><node index="2" text="" resource-id="com.linkedin.android:id/update_detail_comment_bar" class="android.widget.LinearLayout" package="com.linkedin.android" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[0,2856][1440,3120]" drawing-order="3" hint=""><node index="0" text="" resource-id="" class="android.view.View" package="com.linkedin.android" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" 